    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="434bcbc9-b635-5f50-a087-f04e61ec892c" activityNameId="2b4b687f-3aef-5b35-b276-242407597230" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Wind turbine 5MW, offshore, tower</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Wind turbine 5MW, offshore, tower
UUID=cc8c02da-14df-351b-a03a-64f03f0e4f97
Wind turbine tower, at site including manufacturing, transports, installation, replacements, decommission and waste treatement. Calculated for FU of 1p.
Data of material inputs based on the offshore wind turbine REpower 5M, with a nominal capacity of 5 MW, as used in the Ormonde offshore wind farm, UK.
The distance to installation port is assumed to be 187 km.
Assumed lifetime is 25 years.

Main data source regarding material composition: 
Kouloumpis, V., &amp; Azapagic, A. (2022). A model for estimating life cycle environmental impacts of offshore wind electricity considering specific characteristics of wind farms. Sustainable Production and Consumption, 29, 495–506. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spc.2021.10.024
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cc8c02da-14df-351b-a03a-64f03f0e4f97.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
